I wanted to check in about something from today.

While I was working, a man showed up, said he was with the park service, an=
d started taking photos of the yurts while they were still dirty, since I w=
as in the process of cleaning them. I engaged him briefly=97asked if he had=
 any questions=97but the interaction felt a little off.

He didn=92t introduce himself by name, wasn=92t in uniform, and had no visi=
ble identification. He only said he was with the park service and that they=
 =93needed photos of some of them still.=94 Then he started asking me quest=
ions=97how I like the park, how I=92m being treated here. It stood out, esp=
ecially with the timing, since all the rangers were away for meetings.

Was this an official visit that you're aware of? If so, no problem=97just s=
eemed a bit odd, and I wasn=92t sure if I should have handled it differentl=
y. If not, I wanted to flag it in case it=92s something to be aware of. Let=
 me know if you have any insight.

Thanks,
Sam

